\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Stand up and bless the Lord,
\par Ye people of His choice;
\par Stand up and bless the Lord your God,
\par With heart and soul and voice.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Though high above all praise,
\par Above all blessing high,
\par Who would not fear His holy name,
\par And laud and magnify?
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. O for the living flame
\par From His own altar brought,
\par To touch our lips, our minds inspire,
\par And wing to heaven our thought!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. There, with benigh regard
\par Our hymns He deigns to hear;
\par Though unrevealed to mortal sense,
\par Our spirits feel Him near.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. God is our strength and song,
\par And His salvation ours;
\par Then be His love in Christ proclaimed
\par With all our ransomed powers.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. Stand up and bless the Lord,
\par The Lord your God adore;
\par 6. Stand up and bless His glorious name
\par Henceforth for evermore.
\par                 Amen.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

